    <briefdescription>
<para>Binary inet address structure. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It contains two fields at this moment - IP and port encoded as usual numbers. It means that after <ref refid="msgpuck_8h_1a741b3334e42f17c72114c6658bfc696d" kindref="member">mp_decode_uint()</ref> it is necessary to use htonl/htons() functions to assign the values to struct sockaddr_in. </para>    </detaileddescription>
